l3: Re-create a router whose type changed instead of swapping it

The fix for bug 1892846 (489e0ead72) swapped a router whose type
changed for an object that was never initialized, and left the old
router's keepalived, radvd and state change processes running. An IPv6
router then failed in enable_radvd and ran on without radvd.

Delete the stale router and add it again, as the DVR HA branch below
already does, so the new object is initialized before it is processed.

